WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.567
-Our next guest is a beloved
best-selling author

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:06.367
whose books have sold
over 90 million copies

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:08.334
in 39 languages.

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:10.534
A film based on
her breakthrough novel,

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:12.400
"Are You There, God?
It's Me, Margaret,"

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.868
opens in theaters Friday.

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:16.200
Everyone, please welcome
Judy Blume!

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.667
-♪ She's the one ♪

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:22.734
♪ Who likes
all our pretty songs ♪

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:25.567
♪ And she likes to sing along ♪

00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:28.534
♪ And she likes
to shoot her gun ♪

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:32.367
♪ But she don't know
what it means ♪

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.033
♪ Don't know what it means ♪

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:37.133
-Welcome!

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:42.067
I am so excited to have
the Judy Blume here! Yes!

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:44.100
I'm such a fan.
-Thank you.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.734
-When did it all start for you?

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:48.534
You were making picture books.
Is that correct?

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.200
-Yeah, I was
writing picture books.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.901
You know, I had little kids.
I was creative.

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:55.834
I needed creative excitement.
-Yeah.

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:56.968
And so what kind of books?

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:58.901
What would your books be called,
were about?

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:01.801
-Terrible rhyming picture books.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:04.400
Really bad imitation Dr. Seuss.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.667
-Really bad?
-No. [ Laughs ]

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:07.367
-Oh, okay.
Can you give me an example

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.834
of a book that you --
a picture book that you wrote?

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:11.701
-I could.
-Yeah.

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:13.868
-You promise not to fall down?
-Yeah, no.

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:15.634
-If you're laughing.
-I would love it.

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:16.534
-Okay. Okay.
So, this was called

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:21.734
"You, Mom, You."
Not published.

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:24.133
I've told my kids,
"If you ever publish it

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:25.868
after I'm gone, I'll haunt you."

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:27.100
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.567
No. It's called "You, Mom..."?
-"You, Mom, You."

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:32.634
It's about a mother who's trying
to explain to her little kids

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.234
that she was once a kid.

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:36.167
So it goes like this.

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:38.501
"You, Mom, you?
You were a kid.

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:40.601
Tell us,
tell us what you did.

00:01:40.601 --> 00:01:42.801
Okay, okay.
I'll tell you all

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:44.667
the things I did
when I was small."

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:46.467
I think it's, "I suck my thumb,
I loved a bear,

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:47.901
one time,
I cut off all my hair."

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.567
[ Laughter ]
-No. What are you --

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:51.934
Why is that --
Why are you embarrassed?

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:54.167
That's awesome.
-It was terrible.

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:56.801
"You, Mom, You."
-And not only that,

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:59.067
but I illustrated them myself.

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:02.868
And I really do not have
any talent and...

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:04.033
-Yeah, and...

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.701
-And I put them together
with brass fasteners,

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:07.968
you know,
like we did in school.

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:09.701
-Of course.
-Little brass fasteners.

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:12.100
And then I sent them off
to publishing companies.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.334
-And what was their response?

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:16.200
-I got rejections.
-Yeah. Yeah, you did, yeah.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.601
-My favorite rejection was,

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:21.634
"Does not win
in competition with others,"

00:02:21.634 --> 00:02:24.400
from "Highlight" magazine.
-No!

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.033
-Yes!
-"Highlight" magazine?

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:27.834
-I never let my kids
read that magazine.

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:30.968
[ Laughter ]
Never.

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:33.100
-Oh, my goodness. No way.
-Yes.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.167
-But then look at you now.

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:35.534
I mean, how many books
have you done?

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:37.400
Twenty -- 29 books?
-So I hear.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.100
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.701
-"Are You There, God?
It's Me, Margaret."

00:02:40.701 --> 00:02:42.534
"Tales of
a Fourth Grade Nothing" --

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:44.567
my daughter's reading that now.

00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:47.667
"Blubber," "Forever,"
"Superfudge."

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:50.901
These are legendary books.

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:54.100
I remember growing up.
You were in a lot of trouble.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.167
You were, like --
you were banned, I think.

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:57.467
-Were you growing up
in the '80s?

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:58.767
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:58.767 --> 00:03:00.601
-You were banned. I think you
were banned in my house.

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:03.100
My mom didn't
let my sister read you.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.501
-But she did.
-She did.

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:05.801
-She did.
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:07.434
-Of course she did.
-Kids will get what they want.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:08.734
I think she borrowed it --

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:12.300
-All you have to do is say,
"I don't want you..."

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.400
Well, I tell parents,
I say, "Don't tell them

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.133
these were the favorite books
when you were a kid.

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:20.234
Don't tell them that.
They will not want to read them

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:23.767
because mom is not cool.
So this is what you do.

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.701
You put them on tables
and, you know,

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:27.334
you let them look, and you say,

00:03:27.334 --> 00:03:30.801
'Oh, well, I don't think
you're ready for that.'"

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:34.167
-Oh! That's pretty great.
See? Genius.

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:37.467
-Yeah.
[ Applause ]

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:38.767
-There's a documentary
about you, called

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:43.033
"Judy Blume Forever," that's out
right now on Prime Video.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:44.501
And I loved it.

00:03:44.501 --> 00:03:47.567
And I'll tell you the part
that I really -- really got me.

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:49.601
Not only you have
a legendary career,

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:52.467
but you wrote back
to your fan mail,

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:54.868
and you saved your fan mail.

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:56.434
-I did keep all my fan mail.

00:03:56.434 --> 00:04:00.734
Yes. And I'm notoriously --
I throw away everything.

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:01.901
-Yeah.
-Everybody knows

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:03.033
I throw away everything.

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:05.334
But I kept every one
of those letters.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.667
-And it's amazing to watch.

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:09.701
You wrote them back
and have them.

00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:13.000
I mean, you were getting
2,000 a month, fan letters --

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.734
-At one point, yeah.
I didn't write everybody back.

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:16.968
-No, I understand that.

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:19.534
But you kept them, though.
-The ones who needed me.

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:22.033
The ones who needed to hear
from me I wrote back.

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:25.000
-Yeah, and then.
And then there are two girls

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.868
who wrote you
that are in the movie now.

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:28.367
They're in their 50s.

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.968
-And they have their own kids,
teenage kids.

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:32.634
Yeah.
-It's a beautiful thing.

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:33.801
You have to watch it.

00:04:33.801 --> 00:04:36.000
It's just a great documentary.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.100
But now let's talk about
the main event.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:41.200
Out this Friday, "Are you there,
God? It's Me, Margaret"

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:45.200
is finally a movie.
-I know, 53 years later.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.501
But that's my fault.
That's my fault.

00:04:46.501 --> 00:04:48.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:51.300
-Why is it your fault?
-Because I wouldn't sell it.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.834
-You didn't want --
You didn't want to sell it?

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:55.133
-I didn't want -- I didn't think
that it should be a movie.

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:57.334
Not every book
should be a movie,

00:04:57.334 --> 00:05:00.467
and I was concerned about
how it would be done

00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:04.000
for all these years.
And then suddenly, like,

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.033
from the sky,
came the perfect team.

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:08.767
-Yeah.
-And I knew it was.

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:10.968
-Who is the team?

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:14.868
-Kelly Fremon Craig, who wrote
the letter to me and said --

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:17.734
And by the way, she said,

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:19.567
"I have written and directed
a movie called

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:22.767
'The Edge of Seventeen,'"
and I'm like, "What?!"

00:05:22.767 --> 00:05:24.901
-I love that movie.
-I love that movie.

00:05:24.901 --> 00:05:27.167
I saw that movie.
This is --

00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:28.534
What a credential, right?

00:05:28.534 --> 00:05:31.534
Nobody ever came to me before
with such a credential.

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:33.567
And if that were not enough,
she said,

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:37.367
"And my mentor
is James L. Brooks."

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:40.100
-No, James L. Brooks,
the legend.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:42.534
So did they --
Did they try to woo you?

00:05:42.534 --> 00:05:44.334
Did they --
Did they come to Key West?

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:47.033
-They did. They came
to Key West very quickly.

00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:49.400
And you know what
I was most worried about?

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.501
What would I give them
for lunch?

00:05:51.501 --> 00:05:52.701
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God.

00:05:52.701 --> 00:05:54.567
Of course Judy Blume
would worry about that.

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:56.467
-Right!
-You are so funny.

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:57.667
You have such
a great sense of humor.

00:05:57.667 --> 00:05:59.234
And by the way,
you got to be happy.

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:00.868
The movie turned out great.

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:03.067
-The movie is...

00:06:03.067 --> 00:06:05.767
It's a dream come true.
-You're getting great reviews.

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:10.000
-I never -- I never thought
that we could do this,

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.200
that it could be done.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.901
But Kelly and the actors
are incredible.

00:06:14.901 --> 00:06:16.567
-Yeah.
You were telling me backstage,

00:06:16.567 --> 00:06:19.200
you were saying that you --
"I think I'm the only author

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.200
that will say the movie's
better than the book."

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:23.868
-Yeah, I am probably that...
-That's impossible.

00:06:23.868 --> 00:06:26.968
-...but it is in this case...
-In this case.

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:30.000
-...because it's rounded out.
The characters are all there.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.634
-I'm so happy for you.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:32.634 --> 00:06:34.434
Here is a scene from
"Are you There, God?

00:06:34.434 --> 00:06:36.467
It's Me, Margaret."
Take a look.

00:06:36.467 --> 00:06:39.167
-You hold your arms out like
this, and you say, "I must,

00:06:39.167 --> 00:06:41.400
I must, I must increase my bust!

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.868
I must, I must,
I must increase my bust!"

00:06:44.868 --> 00:06:46.133
-Does that really work?

00:06:46.133 --> 00:06:48.300
-I'm living proof.
Now, come on, get up.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.834
Get up, get up, get up!
You'll see.

00:06:50.834 --> 00:06:52.234
Get up.

00:06:52.234 --> 00:06:55.501
I must, I must,
I must increase my bust!

00:06:55.501 --> 00:06:58.267
-I must,
I must increase my bust!

00:06:58.267 --> 00:07:00.968
-Chin up.
-We must, we must,

00:07:00.968 --> 00:07:03.000
we must increase our bust!

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:06.767
We must, we must,
we must increase our bust!

00:07:06.767 --> 00:07:10.601
-"We must, we must,
we must increase our bust!"

00:07:10.601 --> 00:07:12.834
-Shut up!
You're so stupid!

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:14.367
Shut up!
-I feel it working!

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:16.033
-Mom!

00:07:16.033 --> 00:07:18.267
-[ Laughing ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:18.267 --> 00:07:19.667
Come on!

00:07:19.667 --> 00:07:21.901
Judy Blume, everybody!

00:07:21.901 --> 00:07:23.634
"Are You There, God?
It's Me, Margaret"

00:07:23.634 --> 00:07:25.300
hits theaters Friday.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:26.601
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:07:26.601 --> 00:07:28.334
Stick around.
Thank you so much.

